Context [text box]
Type in the context of the data you want to import. The context designates the node of the structure of the
XML document at which the XMLInterface starts reading data.
Remarks
You might, for example, type in the names of certain data, or of certain objects that you are interested in,
for example Data/Objects.
This way you can restrict the data to be read, i.e., if you do not need to work with all of the data contained
in the XML file, you will specify a context.
If you do not type in a context, the XMLInterface imports the entire file, which may contain a large amount
of data, some of which you do not need. This might take some time to import and use up a large amount
of your computer’s RAM.
